{"id": "EUVD-2026-59200", "enisaUuid": "85658a89-d68e-3c8f-aeba-7803a19c1d7e", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nASoC: SOF: ipc3-control: Fix TOCTOU in bytes_put and bytes_get\n\nIn sof_ipc3_bytes_put(), the size used for the memcpy is derived from\nthe old data->size already in the buffer, not the incoming new data's\nsize field. If the new data has a different size, the copy length is\nwrong: it may truncate valid data or copy stale bytes.\n\nSimilarly, sof_ipc3_bytes_get() checks data->size against max_size\nwithout accounting for the sizeof(struct sof_ipc_ctrl_data) offset\nof the flex array within the allocation.\n\nFix bytes_put to validate and use the incoming data's sof_abi_hdr.size\nfrom ucontrol before copying. Fix bytes_get to subtract sizeof(*cdata)\nfrom the bounds check to match the actual available space.", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:55:20", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T18:55:16", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8bd715a9d882fe1993bb2aec5eff89fffa946592", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0dce240145f47545d2e4b18c6d58033b83e1fd0e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ed4f758f34be4c32e02933ac4fa044589d9c1c16", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0c4fbdaca225b97122b61b68c5353caa33a253c3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/92f90917413bdd6078fefff6f6c83a07bf870b04", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1f97760417b5faa60e9642fd0ed61eb17d0b1b39"], "aliases": ["GHSA-m237-j8mr-f2gj", "CVE-2026-72301"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0292f30c-c241-356f-a527-bcbc9fd11115", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "544ac8858f249950b4d99c68e538cdc07300528f <0dce240145f47545d2e4b18c6d58033b83e1fd0e"}, {"id": "20bd6c0b-0357-372d-aecb-26c6abd2af23", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "544ac8858f249950b4d99c68e538cdc07300528f <8bd715a9d882fe1993bb2aec5eff89fffa946592"}, {"id": "4a05ea2b-03da-3173-9d79-1c977a4395a9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.5"}, {"id": "4c5c726a-8afc-3fa1-8fb1-2a4f91db3cab", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "544ac8858f249950b4d99c68e538cdc07300528f <0c4fbdaca225b97122b61b68c5353caa33a253c3"}, {"id": "5b745035-7474-335c-9d71-a87334d9ad0d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "544ac8858f249950b4d99c68e538cdc07300528f <ed4f758f34be4c32e02933ac4fa044589d9c1c16"}, {"id": "6f122290-8700-3af6-9eee-d33843bcfe41", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "870946d7-b8b2-3b9b-81cf-2edcde6b8b74", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "544ac8858f249950b4d99c68e538cdc07300528f <92f90917413bdd6078fefff6f6c83a07bf870b04"}, {"id": "95fdbe0e-4625-359e-b335-963c319b7090", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.18"}, {"id": "9c709f75-b9a5-3dd4-aeef-05d275b870cf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.97"}, {"id": "b464c414-507b-3d50-9743-f47344b560f5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.40"}, {"id": "c5af3ae3-5b6d-3dbd-8b45-902110b9ecd3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.145"}, {"id": "c7a68cc1-09ad-3011-931f-fc978ab53adf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.178"}, {"id": "d41454dc-10f6-3dbc-8af3-99b04e3e2807", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "544ac8858f249950b4d99c68e538cdc07300528f <1f97760417b5faa60e9642fd0ed61eb17d0b1b39"}, {"id": "f8a50540-ddc0-3537-a6d2-b064b177f943", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vend